@SolidClass base(NuclideIO, BrushCompile, BulwarkScripted) color(128 128 128) = trigger_changelevel : "A trigger volume that initiates a level change, from one map to the next. It can be used in combination with info_landmark and trigger_transition to define a shared point and a transition area for entities respectively. Notes: When a `landmark` is specified, you will have to position two info_landmark entities across your two levels with the same name. They'll mark a translation point for the coordinates in your levels. If you have set a landmark, you might also want to restrict the area in which entities get carried across to the next level. This is accomplished by placing a trigger_transition volume with the same name as the specified `landmark`. If you do not make use of the trigger_transition entity, it will carry over all of the entities that are in the same PVS (room and attached hallways) of the info_landmark. The PVS-culling method can prove difficult to work with. Developers have been spotted using 'killtarget' on entities before level transitions take place to manually filter through them (Half-Life's c1a0e - c1a0c)."
[
	targetname(target_source) : "Targetname" : "" : "Name"
	map(string) : "Map" : "" : "Next .bsp file name to transition to."
	landmark(string) : "Landmark" : "" : "Landmark name to target."
	changedelay(string) : "Changedelay" : "" : "Time in seconds until the transition happens."
	spawnflags(flags) =
	[
		1 : "NO_INTERMISSION" : 0 : "Don't show intermission cam (unimplemented)."
		2 : "TRIGGER_ONLY" : 0 : "Can't activate through touching, only via triggers."
	]
	input ChangeLevel(void) : "Triggers the level to change."
	output OnChangeLevel(void) : "Fired when the level changes."
]

